# D23. claude G-D-03: the shipped topology of a cancel during the image pass,
# under the real timeout rather than the harness's shim. GNU timeout puts
# itself and the helper in a process group of their own, so the interface's
# SIGINT to the run's group reaches the ctl and not the helper; the ctl's INT
# trap stamps CANCELLED, and its EXIT trap ends the helper by SIGTERM
# through timeout. The run is started as the interface starts it -- a
# session and a process group of its own (setsid) -- and the stand-in sends
# the group SIGINT itself.
